WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.360
Settle in a position that is safe and reasonably supported.

2
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:11.770
The eyes may close, soften, or stay open.

3
00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:15.470
There is no need to become still.

4
00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:19.170
Small adjustments are welcome.

5
00:00:24.194 --> 00:00:29.074
Begin with the places where the body meets a surface.

6
00:00:30.774 --> 00:00:36.424
Notice pressure, temperature, firmness, or perhaps very little.

7
00:00:38.124 --> 00:00:42.799
You do not need to name the right sensation.

8
00:00:44.499 --> 00:00:46.419
Simply let contact be known.

9
00:00:52.448 --> 00:00:53.928
Bring attention to the feet.

10
00:00:55.628 --> 00:01:00.638
Feel both feet together, or one at a time.

11
00:01:02.338 --> 00:01:08.183
Notice toes, soles, heels, and the space around them.

12
00:01:09.883 --> 00:01:18.158
If the feet are difficult to sense, feel the socks, shoes, floor, or air instead.

13
00:01:25.694 --> 00:01:31.904
Let attention include the lower legs, knees, and upper legs.

14
00:01:33.604 --> 00:01:40.669
Sensation may be clear, faint, pleasant, unpleasant, or neutral.

15
00:01:42.369 --> 00:01:44.129
Nothing has to change.

16
00:01:45.829 --> 00:01:51.029
Notice the weight of the legs and how they are being supported.

17
00:02:00.073 --> 00:02:04.358
Move toward the pelvis, abdomen, and lower back.

18
00:02:06.058 --> 00:02:12.958
The breath may create movement here, or it may not be obvious.

19
00:02:14.658 --> 00:02:16.658
Let the breath remain natural.

20
00:02:18.358 --> 00:02:24.303
Feel one whole region rather than searching for a special experience.

21
00:02:33.346 --> 00:02:35.586
Include the chest and upper back.

22
00:02:37.286 --> 00:02:42.981
Notice clothing, warmth, movement, or stillness.

23
00:02:44.681 --> 00:02:55.121
If this area feels uncomfortable, return to a steady point of contact such as the feet or seat.

24
00:02:56.821 --> 00:02:59.781
You choose where attention rests.

25
00:03:07.317 --> 00:03:10.157
Feel both hands.

26
00:03:11.857 --> 00:03:16.652
Notice fingers, palms, and the backs of the hands.

27
00:03:18.352 --> 00:03:24.812
Let the arms join the picture, from wrists through elbows to shoulders.

28
00:03:26.512 --> 00:03:29.032
The shoulders do not need to drop.

29
00:03:30.732 --> 00:03:34.622
They can simply be felt as they are.

30
00:03:43.666 --> 00:03:47.841
Bring attention to the neck, jaw, and face.

31
00:03:49.541 --> 00:03:55.946
Notice the mouth, eyes, forehead, and scalp without asking them to relax.

32
00:03:57.646 --> 00:04:03.326
Allow expressions and sensations to be present without correction.

33
00:04:10.862 --> 00:04:20.802
Now sense the body as a whole: contact below, space around, breath moving somewhere within.

34
00:04:22.502 --> 00:04:26.792
Some areas may stand out and others may remain quiet.

35
00:04:28.492 --> 00:04:29.652
Both belong.

36
00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:41.220
Notice one sound in the room.

37
00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:47.055
Let the eyes take in light and shape.

38
00:04:48.755 --> 00:05:00.000
Make the next movement at a comfortable pace, carrying this broader sense of the body with you.
